  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nDry conditions are expected through Friday. An upper level low will\nbring showers and thunderstorms to the region over the weekend. There\nwill be the potential for some slow moving storms and heavy rain at\ntimes over the weekend. There is uncertainty on how quickly this \nsystem moves out of the area. There will be the potential for off and\non precipitation chances into the middle of next week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\n\nBelow normal to near normal temperatures are expected. CAA will be\npresent today and Thursday. Temperatures will warm slightly for \nFriday, but then a return to some 70s for highs on Saturday and \nSunday with cloud cover and rain. Temperatures will climb slightly \nnext week, however these temperatures will be close to normal values\nfor this time of year.",
